Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.12,0:00:03.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hey team.\N嘿，团队们。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.80,0:00:06.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh, gee.\N哦，天哪。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.64,0:00:09.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Are we late?\N我们迟到吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.52,0:00:11.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Guys, good to be here.\N各位，很高兴来到这里。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.88,0:00:12.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Go America.\N为美国加油。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.56,0:00:13.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Go America.\N为美国加油。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.52,0:00:14.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,Team America.\N美国队。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.58,0:00:16.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,.com Yes, indeed.\N.com 没错，确实如此。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.56,0:00:21.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, America, Wright brothers, first man on the moon, the internet.\N所以，美国，莱特兄弟，首次登月，互联网。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.56,0:00:23.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,The two of us, Wright brothers.\N我们两人，就像莱特兄弟一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.28,0:00:24.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,I like that.\N我喜欢这个说法。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.72,0:00:25.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Indeed.\N确实如此。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.60,0:00:30.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've We've essentially led every major technological revolution.\N我们实际上引领了每一次重大的技术革命。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.24,0:00:34.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Which has been to the enormous benefit of America, ordinary Americans,\N这给美国以及普通美国人带来了巨大好处。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.84,0:00:39.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,where I guess we're now calling the super intelligence, which I think is actually good branding.\N我们现在称之为超级智能，我认为这其实是个很好的品牌定位。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.47,0:00:46.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, let's let's talk about how America wins this, and we make that winning good for ordinary Americans.\N那么，让我们来谈谈美国如何赢得这场竞争，以及如何让这种胜利惠及普通美国人。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.84,0:00:50.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, um excuse me, Diet Coke.\N呃，不好意思，我想要一杯健怡可乐。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.00,0:00:52.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sorry.\N对不起。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.56,0:01:01.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,I So, first of all, artificial super intelligence super intelligence I it is a a complete reinvention of the computing stack.\N首先，人工超级智能，它实际上是对计算架构的一次彻底重构。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.85,0:01:07.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh everything from the way the processors, the chips are are designed and the way they operate,\N从处理器和芯片的设计方式，到它们的运行机制，
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.11,0:01:11.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,to the way software is uh now trained and and developed,\N到软件如今的训练和开发方式，
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.53,0:01:17.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,to the way that the applications are able to perform what they're able to do and how they how they perform.\N到应用程序能够执行的任务及其执行方式。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.33,0:01:20.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every single layer of the computing stack has been reinvented.\N计算架构的每一层都已被重新发明。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.68,0:01:26.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um this way of doing computing, unlike previous ways of retrieving information,\N这种计算方式与以往的信息检索方式截然不同。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.40,0:01:33.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,this is a generative approach to to a computing and therefore, in order for us to succeed, the first thing we need is energy.\N这是一种生成式计算方法，因此为了取得成功，我们首先需要能源。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.16,0:01:41.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because we need the energies to to uh run the compute the compute run the algorithms the algorithms um then feed uh the applications.\N因为我们需要能源来运行计算，计算运行算法，算法再为应用提供支持。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.01,0:01:48.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, at the at the foundational layer is energy, and uh from that energy we build the land power and shell,\N因此，在最基础的层面就是能源，而从能源出发，我们构建土地、电力和厂房。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.11,0:01:51.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,and that hosts the infrastructure so on and so forth.\N这些要素承载着基础设施，以此类推。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.06,0:01:58.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, the way we win, um of course, uh we are world-class in chip design, we're world-class in algorithm development.\N我们取胜的方式当然在于，我们在芯片设计方面处于世界领先水平，在算法开发方面也处于世界领先水平。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.03,0:02:07.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and uh so one of the things that we need to do is just be vigilant about enabling power delivery and power generation happen.\N因此，我们需要做的一件事就是持续关注，确保电力输送和发电能够顺利实现。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.84,0:02:12.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And President Trump has been has been visionary in being pro-energy.\N特朗普总统在能源政策上一直具有远见。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.28,0:02:17.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Without the pro-energy vision of President Trump, it would have been impossible for us to build the data centers on top of it.\N如果没有特朗普总统的能源远见，我们根本无法在这一基础上建设数据中心。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.56,0:02:22.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um now, of course, these data centers are coming online so quickly.\N当然，这些数据中心正在迅速投入运行。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.73,0:02:26.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um we're we're coming into a lot of neighborhoods and a lot of communities.\N我们正进入许多社区和居民区。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.92,0:02:31.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have to do a better job um in partnering with the communities and and um make\N我们必须更好地与社区合作，让他们参与进来。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.94,0:02:37.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,and bring them along and make them part of the prosperity and the success of this industrial revolution.\N让他们共同分享这场工业革命带来的繁荣与成功。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.46,0:02:39.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but you know, that's how we win.\N但你知道，这就是我们取胜的方式。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.20,0:02:40.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, we got to build the world's best chips.\N你知道，我们必须打造世界顶尖的芯片。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.00,0:02:46.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,We got to build We have to have lots and lots of energy, uh create incredible algorithms, and then lastly,\N我们必须拥有大量能源，开发出令人惊叹的算法，最后，
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.55,0:02:50.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,make sure that America is enthusiastic about the technology so that we\N确保美国对这项技术充满热情，从而
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.34,0:02:54.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,diffuse it into all of these various industries from manufacturing to health care,\N将其推广到从制造到医疗保健等各个行业，
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.90,0:02:58.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, space uh space exploration, so on and so forth.\N比如太空探索等等。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.56,0:02:59.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Awesome.\N太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.19,0:03:00.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Elon, how do we win?\N埃隆，我们该如何取胜？
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.66,0:03:04.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do we keep winning?\N我们该如何持续取胜？
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.48,0:03:12.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, we need um a lot of power, a lot of uh energy uh generation.\N我们需要大量的电力，大量的能源生产。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.83,0:03:17.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, uh scaling energy I think is is one of the biggest things.\N所以，我认为扩大能源规模是最重要的事情之一。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.79,0:03:21.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,You've got to scale energy, you've got to scale chip production.\N你必须扩大能源规模，也必须扩大芯片生产规模。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.16,0:03:27.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and I I think we're we're winning on software, um on anything intellectual or digital.\N嗯，我觉得我们在软件、任何智力或数字领域都在取得胜利。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.81,0:03:30.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but uh long run in the long run,\N但说到底，从长远来看，
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.92,0:03:39.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,we need to be able to generate enough power uh to compete with uh I think essentially China is the biggest competitor.\N我们需要能够产生足够的电力，以应对竞争，我认为本质上中国是最大的竞争对手。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.96,0:03:45.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and China has um about three times the electricity production of the United States.\N而且中国的电力产量大约是美国的三倍。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.52,0:03:48.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and I think we'll figure out how to make chips.\N嗯，我想我们会找到制造芯片的方法。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.28,0:03:52.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, so the the really the the central challenge,\N所以，真正核心的挑战是
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.01,0:03:58.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,think is long long-term is going to be how do you generate enough power and how do you ensure\N长期来看，关键是如何产生足够的电力，以及如何确保电力供应。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.23,0:04:04.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,that uh we have enough uh logic and memory fabrication capacity in the United States or in a safe region?\N我们美国或安全地区是否有足够的逻辑和内存制造产能？
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.52,0:04:06.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, you are We need the Wright brothers on the job.\N好吧，我们需要莱特兄弟来接手这项工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.04,0:04:08.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.12,0:04:10.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, turns out the Wright brothers are on the job.\N原来莱特兄弟正在处理这件事。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.34,0:04:19.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,Elon, if you bring on 10 gigawatts, which SpaceX has has discussed publicly, that'll be about 25% of all the power added in America.\N埃隆，如果你能引入10吉瓦的电力，这正是SpaceX公开讨论过的规模，\N那将占美国新增电力总量的约25%。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.47,0:04:24.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I know you have literal rocket engineers working on bringing on the power.\N我知道你们真的有火箭工程师在负责供电事宜。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.62,0:04:24.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.96,0:04:26.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Help you make the turbines.\N帮你制造涡轮机。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.28,0:04:29.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, can you can you talk about that?\N那你能谈谈这个吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.24,0:04:36.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, it's I mean just to to to frame this, um the average power consumption in the United States is about 500 gigawatts.\N对，简单来说，美国的平均电力消耗约为500吉瓦。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.80,0:04:43.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, every 5 gigawatts of incremental steady-state production is a 1% increase in in the power used.\N因此，每增加5吉瓦的稳定电力产能，就相当于电力使用量增加1%。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.96,0:04:50.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh And and I think actually will materialize to be approximately 1% increase in GDP.\N我认为这实际上会带来约1%的GDP增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.68,0:04:53.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um because the the intelligence per watt keeps increasing.\N因为每瓦特的智能产出持续提升。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.95,0:05:00.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, if you just, you know, plot on a curve, um how is how is the useful intelligence per watt increasing?\N所以，如果你画出一条曲线，看看每瓦特的有用智能是如何提升的？
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.96,0:05:10.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um how is the both at the hardware level, adjacents uh GPUs keep getting better in terms of their the their you know, the the com- compute per watt.\N硬件层面，像GPU这类相邻组件在每瓦特算力方面持续进步。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.80,0:05:16.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and the uh algorithms also get better in using it in getting more intelligence per watt.\N同时，算法也在不断优化，让每瓦特的智能产出更高。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.96,0:05:20.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, uh So, I I think that's a maybe an interesting note.\N所以，我认为这可能是个有趣的观察点。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.71,0:05:26.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I I I would bet anyone that 1% increase in power usage corresponds to roughly 1% increase in GDP.\N我敢打赌，电力使用量每增加1%，GDP大约也会增加1%。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.83,0:05:30.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and so, 10 10 gigawatts would be a 2% increase in in GDP.\N所以，10吉瓦的电力将带来GDP约2%的增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.92,0:05:33.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um with with the Rubins, I think.\N嗯，用鲁宾（Rubins）来算的话，我觉得。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.79,0:05:35.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um So, Well, let's do let's do the simple math.\N嗯，那我们来算个简单的数学题。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.04,0:05:45.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, each gigawatt um can probably generate about, call it, 40 50 billion dollars of economic output each year.\N每吉瓦大概每年能产生约400亿到500亿美元的经济产出。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.88,0:05:50.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh yeah, I mean well, 1% would be Yeah, I mean Yeah.\N嗯，是的，1%的话就是……嗯，是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.12,0:05:53.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,1% in the United States would be 300 billion.\N美国1%的增量相当于3000亿美元。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.68,0:05:55.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, 300 billion.\N对，3000亿美元。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.53,0:05:57.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, 50 1/6.\N那么，50除以6。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.08,0:06:05.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Wha- 1% of the of the 1% increase, so 5 gigawatts would be Yeah, well, 5 gigawatts gigawatts would be 300 billion.\N等等，是1%的1%的增量，所以5吉瓦相当于……嗯，5吉瓦就是3000亿美元。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.40,0:06:07.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Exactly, 60 60 billion gigawatts.\N完全正确，600亿吉瓦。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.17,0:06:07.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.48,0:06:08.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.32,0:06:10.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,The math maths.\N数学。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.12,0:06:10.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.80,0:06:11.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.48,0:06:12.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's what we're good at.\N这正是我们擅长的。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.64,0:06:13.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.16,0:06:13.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.68,0:06:15.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.68,0:06:20.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, so that's that's a quite a bit Not good at too many other things, but math.\N所以，这正是我们擅长的，其他很多方面都不太行，但数学除外。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.40,0:06:25.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um Yeah, I mean, it's it's going to increase quite dramatically year over year.\N嗯，我的意思是，它将逐年大幅增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.80,0:06:34.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, so Yeah, I mean Th- Th- Th- Th- From a SpaceX standpoint, we're looking at the long term,\N嗯，从太空探索公司（SpaceX）的角度来看，我们着眼于长远。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.68,0:06:39.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,how do we access a lot more energy than could be accessed on the ground.\N我们如何获取比地面多得多的能量？
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.28,0:06:40.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and that's with space.\N而且这还涉及太空。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.04,0:06:44.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, uh, orbital compute is going to be a very big deal.\N所以，呃，轨道算力将会是一件非常重要的事情。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.52,0:06:46.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um In fact, and and Google agrees.\N呃，事实上，谷歌也同意这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.27,0:06:52.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,They they just actually sent up, uh or either about to or or so- soon or soon about to send up some TPUs.\N他们刚刚实际发射了，呃，或者即将，或者很快就要发射一些TPU。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.65,0:06:58.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think there's there was a um an H100 that was put into orbit like last year, I think.\N我觉得去年应该有一块H100被送入了轨道，我记得是这样。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.40,0:06:58.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.92,0:07:02.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so, it it does work in in space.\N呃，所以它在太空中确实能运行。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.12,0:07:11.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um And and and SpaceX is aiming together with Tesla to do 200 gigawatts of solar uh production per year.\N而且呃，SpaceX正与特斯拉合作，目标是每年实现200吉瓦的太阳能生产。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.76,0:07:18.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,And if brought to space, that you you get the nameplate or better on on the solar power, whereas if it's on the ground,\N如果放到太空中，太阳能的额定功率或更高，而如果在地面上，
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.29,0:07:24.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,you're going to get somewhere between a fifth and an eighth of the uh solar power generation, and you need enormous batteries.\N你只能获得大约五分之一到八分之一的太阳能发电量，而且需要巨大的电池。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.64,0:07:29.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, where- whereas it's uh essentially always sunny in space,\N所以，相比之下，太空中基本上总是阳光充足，
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.18,0:07:38.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,so uh And right now is a great time to do it because the economic returns of these computing systems are so good that the the launch cost,\N所以现在正是绝佳时机，因为这些计算系统的经济回报如此之高，以至于发射成本，
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.66,0:07:45.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,although it's still quite high, um in terms of the overall economic benefit is quite quite affordable.\N虽然成本仍然很高，但从整体经济效益来看，已经相当实惠了。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.84,0:07:47.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Absolutely. the perfect time to do it.\N完全正确，现在正是最佳时机。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.84,0:07:50.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Putting NVIDIA computing in space is the best way to get there.\N将英伟达的计算能力送入太空，是实现这一目标的最佳途径。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.76,0:07:55.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, climbing the curvature of skill with American power and American chips on American rockets.\N没错，借助美国的科技实力和美国芯片，搭载美国火箭，不断突破技能曲线。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.40,0:07:55.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,I love it.\N我太喜欢了。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.92,0:07:56.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.40,0:08:04.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, Jensen, you said something that I thought was important to about how when we bring the energy to all these small towns,\N所以，黄仁勋，你刚才提到的一点我认为很重要，就是当我们把能源带到这些小城镇时，
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.05,0:08:07.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,we're re-industrializing America.\N我们正在重振美国的工业。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.32,0:08:09.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're revitalizing small towns.\N我们正在复兴小城镇。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.10,0:08:10.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're modernizing the grid.\N我们正在升级电网。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.77,0:08:17.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,These are things that essentially every American politician has wanted for the last 35 years.\N这些正是过去35年来几乎所有美国政客都想要实现的目标。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.52,0:08:18.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,What would you say?\N你有什么看法？
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.48,0:08:24.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,What what what are some specifics you can give about how data centers are\N数据中心的具体情况你能说说哪些方面？
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.59,0:08:29.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,good for ordinary Americans and the communities and how they're getting better for those communities.\N对普通美国人及其社区都有利，也让这些社区变得越来越好。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.36,0:08:30.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, we used to call them data centers.\N是的，我们过去管它们叫数据中心。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.92,0:08:33.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,We call them data centers because that's where we hold data.\N我们称它们为数据中心，因为那里是我们存放数据的地方。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.90,0:08:39.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,But, the things that we're building now, these are really SI factories, super intelligence factories.\N但我们正在构建的东西，实际上是超级智能工厂，也就是超级智能工厂。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.52,0:08:42.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason why it's a factory is because you're producing something of economic value.\N之所以称之为工厂，是因为你在生产具有经济价值的东西。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.92,0:08:44.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're just not storing it.\N你只是没有储存它。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.88,0:08:49.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so uh these SI factories um are real factories.\N所以啊，这些超级智能工厂确实是真正的工厂。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.80,0:08:52.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's like a you know, big giant power generator and a real factory.\N就像一个巨大的发电机组，又像一个真正的工厂。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.74,0:08:56.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's got a lot of computing and then networking in there, power generation, cooling systems.\N里面有很多计算资源，还有网络、发电和冷却系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.80,0:08:58.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's complicated things.\N情况很复杂。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.14,0:09:04.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, we're building out, you know, just as the internet today allows you to find anything anywhere,\N因此，我们正在构建的，就像今天的互联网让你能够随时随地找到任何信息一样，
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.78,0:09:12.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,in the future with these AI excuse me, SI infrastructure, SI factories, you'll be able to know anything and do anything from anywhere.\N未来，有了这些AI基础设施和超级智能工厂，你将能够随时随地了解任何事物并完成任何任务。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.88,0:09:21.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, uh now, we're building this infrastructure out and call it across all of the United States,\N因此，我们现在正在全美范围内建设这一基础设施。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.28,0:09:25.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,somewhere between 10 20 gigawatts a year, let's just just estimate.\N每年大约10到20吉瓦，我们就这么估算一下。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.42,0:09:31.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,That creates just you know, probably about a million jobs in in building out these data centers.\N这仅在建设数据中心方面，就可能创造约一百万个就业岗位。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.74,0:09:35.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Don't forget you've got to build the power generation plants, you've got to build the data centers,\N别忘了，你还需要建设发电厂，建设数据中心，
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.38,0:09:40.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,you've got construction, you've got you know, power cooling, you've got, you know, pipe fitters.\N还需要建筑施工，需要电力冷却，还需要管道工。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.36,0:09:45.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, this is the first time in probably, as you mentioned, 35, I was going to say 50 years.\N这可能是自你提到的35年前，甚至50年来第一次。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.48,0:09:52.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,First time in 50 years, we are re-industrializing the United States, creating a whole bunch of blue-collar jobs.\N50年来，我们首次正在重新工业化美国，创造出大量蓝领工作岗位。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.25,0:10:01.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um I And I think we want we want an econ we want an economy that has a shape that includes white-collar jobs and blue-collar jobs,\N我认为，我们想要的经济，应该是一个既包含白领工作也包含蓝领工作的结构，
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.62,0:10:03.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,not just white-collar jobs.\N而不仅仅是白领工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.14,0:10:13.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, so I think that this is our great chance of reshaping our economy and bringing that type of builders and craft uh back into the United States.\N因此，我认为这是我们重塑经济的绝佳机会，将这类工匠和建造者重新带回美国。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.48,0:10:14.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Absolutely.\N完全正确。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.76,0:10:21.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it I mean, it feels like what uh what what Colossus and MacroHard and MacroHarder have done have been amazing.\N而且我觉得，科洛苏斯和宏硬以及更宏硬所做的事情真的太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.04,0:10:24.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,The communities around them, the jobs they've created.\N他们所带动的社区，以及创造的就业岗位。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.25,0:10:26.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do you How do you think about that?\N你如何看待这一点？
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.56,0:10:31.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh yeah, the I mean, the economic impact is a positive economic impact has been tremendous.\N嗯，经济影响是积极的，而且影响非常巨大。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.08,0:10:36.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I mean, we we have there's actually a job shortage in in the region.\N事实上，这个地区正面临劳动力短缺。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.38,0:10:44.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,And whereas there used to be quite a bit of unemployment, and now it's uh there's there's there's a overemployment, if you will.\N过去失业率很高，现在则出现了某种程度的过热就业，可以说。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.08,0:10:46.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's There's more jobs than than there are people.\N就业岗位比人多。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.76,0:10:51.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and the the tax benefits uh for the community have been tremendous.\N社区获得的税收优惠也非常可观。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.32,0:10:55.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think they're I think we might have doubled their their tax budget or something.\N我觉得我们的税收预算可能翻了一番，或者差不多。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.79,0:10:57.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um quite quite tremendous.\N真是相当惊人。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.32,0:11:04.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we we do like small things that are helpful, like provide, you know, low-priced uh half-priced darling uh access.\N我们也做一些小而有用的事，比如提供低价，甚至半价的达伦访问权限。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.88,0:11:07.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um we're building a water recycling plant.\N我们正在建设一座水循环利用厂。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.29,0:11:10.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's a $250 million water recycling plant.\N这是一个耗资2.5亿美元的水循环利用厂。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.20,0:11:12.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I think you you do need to do things for the community.\N嗯，我认为你们确实需要为社区做些事情。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.65,0:11:14.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and if you do so, they will reciprocate.\N嗯，如果你们这样做了，他们也会回报你们。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.00,0:11:15.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Awesome.\N太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.56,0:11:21.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, one of the the things that people people forget is that for the first time in in probably forever,\N现在，人们常常忘记的一点是，可能是有史以来第一次，
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.72,0:11:27.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,that we have the market forces to support the investment of sustainable energy.\N市场力量正在支持可持续能源的投资。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.15,0:11:34.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,You give me an example of a fusion, fission, you know, small nuclear reactor, large reactor.\N给我一个核聚变、核裂变，或者小型、大型核反应堆的例子。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.13,0:11:37.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Almost every form of sustainable energy is being funded today.\N如今，几乎所有形式的可持续能源都在获得资金支持。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.56,0:11:45.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so we have the opportunity to fund the future of energy without without the government subsidizing without right I\N因此，我们有机会资助能源的未来，而无需政府补贴，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.08,0:11:51.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,mean we this is you give me an example of a great energy battery storage idea it's going to get funded.\N我的意思是，你给我举个优秀的能源电池储能方案，它就会获得资助。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.72,0:11:52.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Awesome.\N太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.68,0:11:55.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,By the way, on behalf of all Americans I want to thank both of you.\N顺便说一句，代表所有美国人，我想感谢你们两位。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.49,0:12:01.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think combined you have created more than 5 trillion dollars of wealth for ordinary Americans in their 401 Ks.\N我认为你们两人共同为普通美国人的401(k)账户创造了超过5万亿美元的财富。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.00,0:12:05.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Tens of thousands, maybe hundreds of thousands of jobs directly.\N直接创造了数万，或许数十万个工作岗位。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.52,0:12:07.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Many tens of billions of wages.\N数十亿美元的工资。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.36,0:12:14.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,So thank you.\N所以谢谢你们。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.96,0:12:17.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think Jensen's done 5 trillion by himself actually.\N其实我觉得黄仁勋一个人就创造了5万亿美元。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.44,0:12:17.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.\N对不起。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.00,0:12:21.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think Jensen's done 5 trillion by himself.\N我觉得黄仁勋一个人就创造了5万亿美元。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.76,0:12:25.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think I'm I'm thinking I'm like around 3 and 1/2 or something.\N我觉得我大概在3500亿左右，差不多这样。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.84,0:12:29.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,I was trying to I was trying to be conservative.\N我当时是想保守一点估算。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.32,0:12:31.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you guys You guys both had a great Monday.\N所以你们俩今天周一都表现得非常出色。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.98,0:12:35.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,I was watching the Starship launch.\N我在观看星舰发射。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.44,0:12:44.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,First orbital Starship launch while I was reading about the open agent safety framework from Nvidia which was an exciting morning.\N在阅读英伟达发布的开放智能体安全框架时，恰逢星舰首次轨道发射，真是令人兴奋的一天。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.64,0:12:48.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,So maybe maybe maybe you could each talk about each of those because\N所以也许你们每人可以分别谈谈这些点
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.29,0:12:53.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,we need Starship to get those 200 gigawatts of American solar with American chips,\N我们需要星舰将200吉瓦的美国太阳能和美国芯片
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.88,0:12:57.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,American super intelligence into orbit.\N以及美国超级智能送入轨道
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.60,0:12:59.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'll talk about his and he talks about mine.\N我来谈他的，他来谈我的
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.60,0:13:01.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,No, I'm just kidding.\N不，我开玩笑的
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.44,0:13:03.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,So so let's see.\N那么，我们来看看
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.75,0:13:07.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,As you know, we want to advance AI advance SI.\N如你们所知，我们希望推进AI，推进超级智能
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.13,0:13:08.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,We I'm going to get good at this.\N我会在这方面变得越来越熟练
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.95,0:13:14.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're going to advance SI in a in a responsible and optimistic way.\N我们将以负责任且乐观的方式推进超级智能
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.90,0:13:22.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we we know that the future we strongly believe that the future that SI is going to enable is a future that we want to be part of.\N我们坚信，超级智能将开启的未来，正是我们希望参与其中的未来
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.53,0:13:25.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so we're optimistic about that and that's the reason why we're driving so hard.\N因此我们对此充满乐观，这也是我们如此努力的原因
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.61,0:13:29.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,On the other hand, we have to make sure that we develop this technology safely and securely.\N另一方面，我们必须确保以安全和可靠的方式发展这项技术
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.50,0:13:31.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, there's several different parts of it.\N嗯，它有几个不同的部分。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.51,0:13:39.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,While you're training the model, um, that's that's generally a fairly safe environment, but while you're evaluating the model,\N在训练模型时，嗯，这通常是一个相对安全的环境，但在评估模型时，
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.05,0:13:46.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,while you're testing the model, you have to make sure that the agent agentic system, the model itself, is highly contained.\N在测试模型时，你必须确保智能体代理系统和模型本身都高度受控。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.11,0:13:49.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,That containment system has to be really secure.\N这个受控系统必须非常安全。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.96,0:13:52.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the second thing is that while you're while you're testing it,\N第二点是，在测试过程中，
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.00,0:13:57.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,you want to monitor that that just because just even though even though you have a contained,\N你应当监控它，即使你已经实现了受控，
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.77,0:14:01.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,you should never trust that it's contained, and so you want to monitor it in real time.\N你也永远不应完全信任它已被完全控制，因此需要实时监控。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.76,0:14:07.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you want to ideally monitor it with another another chip so that it is outside, you know,\N理想情况下，你应该使用另一块芯片来监控，使其处于外部，你知道，
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.78,0:14:13.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,if you will call out of band, outside the environment, outside the sandbox of the agent itself.\N也就是所谓的带外监控，脱离智能体自身的环境和沙箱。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.00,0:14:17.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, you want to contain, and you want to monitor.\N所以，你既要实现受控，也要进行监控。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.25,0:14:23.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, once you're done evaluating in this way, when you deploy, you want to use a very similar system.\N嗯，一旦以这种方式完成评估，部署时你也应使用非常相似的系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.24,0:14:28.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is no different than than, um, uh, just about any digital any human employee that you hire.\N这和你雇佣任何一位数字员工或人类员工并无不同。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.79,0:14:35.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, you give them a containment of rights and tools and access, uh, and then you monitor on a on a regular basis, on a continuous basis.\N你给他们提供权利、工具和访问权限的隔离环境，然后定期、持续地进行监控。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.64,0:14:43.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, in the case of agents, we just have to make sure containment and monitoring has to be done in the most secure of ways.\N因此，在智能体的情况下，我们必须确保隔离和监控以最安全的方式进行。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.04,0:14:44.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we introduce two technologies.\N我们引入了两项技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.58,0:14:45.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,One's called OpenShell.\N一项叫做 OpenShell。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.95,0:14:48.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, it's a a containment system.\N呀，它是一个隔离系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.39,0:14:53.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, it's basically kind of like a browser for websites.\N呀，它基本上就像一个网站浏览器。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.07,0:14:56.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's now essentially a browser of agents.\N现在它本质上是一个智能体浏览器。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.20,0:15:04.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, and that browser keeps, uh, the agent isolated from the rest of the computer, and the rights that you give it are only the rights it should have.\N呀，这个浏览器将智能体与计算机的其余部分隔离，你赋予它的权限仅限于它应有的权限。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.19,0:15:09.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then the the the monitoring system, uh, is a a new chip called BlueField,\N然后监控系统，呀，是一块名为 BlueField 的新芯片，
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.37,0:15:13.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,and it it keeps an eye on everything that the agent is doing at all times.\N它会持续关注智能体所做的一切。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.39,0:15:18.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,And if it does anything that's, you know, out of bounds and against the policy that has been given,\N如果它做了任何越界或违反已设定策略的事情，
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.52,0:15:22.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh, then it, you know, escalates, uh, as far as you need it to escalate.\N呀，它就会根据需要升级响应。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.52,0:15:25.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I thought it was a great analogy um in in a technical blog where you\N而我认为这是一个很好的类比，出现在一篇技术博客中，你提到
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.80,0:15:30.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,said in the early days of internet everybody was worried about your credit card could get stolen.\N在互联网早期，每个人都担心自己的信用卡会被盗。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.29,0:15:37.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,We made the internet safe and that's why we have Amazon, we have Netflix, we have Google, we have X.\N我们让互联网变得安全了，这才有了亚马逊、有了Netflix、有了谷歌、有了X。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.34,0:15:40.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have so many so many great things cuz we made the internet safe.\N我们拥有这么多伟大的事物，正是因为让互联网变得安全了。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.35,0:15:42.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now we're doing now now we're doing the same with AI.\N现在我们正在对AI做同样的事。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.00,0:15:47.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And safety is not you know, inconsistent with advancing the technology.\N安全性并不意味着与技术进步相矛盾。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.80,0:15:50.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Safety and advancing the technology is one in the same thing.\N安全与推动技术进步本质上是一回事。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.96,0:15:57.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's no different than than uh when you have autopilot, not only is it advanced technology, it's also safer technology.\N这和自动驾驶系统没什么不同，它不仅是先进技术，也是更安全的技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.68,0:16:02.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so you want to you advance the technology in that way um the two are not in conflict.\N所以你应当以这种方式推动技术进步，两者并不冲突。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.99,0:16:08.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um the idea that if you advance capability, it somehow compromises safety.\N认为技术能力提升就会损害安全性的想法。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.39,0:16:10.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you advance safety, somehow you fall behind.\N或者认为加强安全性就会落后于技术发展。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.80,0:16:13.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,That that's just that you know, those are false choices.\N这些都只是错误的二选一选择。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.48,0:16:14.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, safety lets us accelerate.\N是的，安全让我们能够加速推进。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.94,0:16:18.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,But Elon, if the Starship's going to be a big part of those 200 gigawatts,\N但埃隆，如果星舰将成为那200吉瓦中重要的一部分，
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.92,0:16:24.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,what can you tell us about Monday's flight, what you learned, how you feeling about the program?\N你能告诉我们关于周一飞行的情况吗？你学到了什么？对这个项目感觉如何？
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.08,0:16:26.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I think the Starship is going great.\N是的，我认为星舰进展非常顺利。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.08,0:16:34.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we've we we took a Starship to orbit for the first time and we deployed uh Starlink V3 satellites, which were enormous satellites.\N嗯，我们首次将星舰送入了轨道，并部署了星链V3卫星，那些卫星非常巨大。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.66,0:16:38.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, these are satellites with the wingspan of a 737.\N这些卫星的翼展相当于波音737的大小。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.48,0:16:41.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, um really enormous.\N所以，真的非常巨大。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.52,0:16:46.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so it's in fact it's it's the largest payload delivered to orbit since Skylab.\N事实上，这是自天空实验室以来，送入轨道的最大载荷。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.88,0:16:56.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, uh now we expect Starship to uh ultimately next year, I think, probably reach um a weekly or twice weekly cadence.\N所以，我们预计星舰明年最终能达到每周或每两周一次的发射频率。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.24,0:16:58.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've got Tom Brown here.\N汤姆·布朗在这里。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.40,0:17:01.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,I know him by his X handle.\N我通过他的X平台账号认识他。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.95,0:17:03.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Welcome.\N欢迎。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.48,0:17:06.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Good to see you guys again.\N很高兴再次见到你们。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.16,0:17:07.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um It's long overdue.\N唉，早就该见面了。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.40,0:17:09.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, it was.\N是啊，确实如此。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.16,0:17:12.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh my my car took a wrong turn, so you guys got here faster than me.\N唉，我的车走错路了，所以你们比我还快到。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.12,0:17:14.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Impressive.\N非常厉害。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.04,0:17:16.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Glad you made it.\N欢迎你终于到了。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.76,0:17:18.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, but Elon, please please continue.\N那么，埃隆，麻烦你继续讲。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.28,0:17:25.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,You were talking about how Starship is going to let us get to 200 gigs of American solar with American chips with American superintelligence.\N你刚才谈到，星舰将让我们用美国芯片和美国超级智能，实现200吉瓦的美国太阳能。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.84,0:17:27.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, so so I mean Starship is going to do a lot of things.\N是的，星舰将完成很多事情。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.78,0:17:34.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's I mean it's intended uh to uh carry enough payload to the moon and Mars to build a self-growing city on the moon and Mars.\N它的设计目标是能将足够多的载荷运送到月球和火星，以在月球和火星上建立一个自我扩展的城市。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.04,0:17:38.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, um but I think as a rough order of magnitude,\N所以，大致估算一下，
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.57,0:17:46.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,you need about a million tons to deliver to the surface of the moon to uh create a self-growing city or similarly a sort of similar number for Mars.\N你需要大约一百万吨物资运送到月球表面，才能建立一个自我扩展的城市，火星也类似，需要差不多的数量。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.04,0:17:54.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and and and then in addition it will launch um at least 300 gigawatts a year of uh AI compute.\N而且除此之外，它每年还将至少新增300吉瓦的AI算力。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.56,0:18:02.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um that 200 gigawatts a year would be a 40% increase annually in the United States total energy uh consumption.\N每年200吉瓦的算力，相当于美国总能源消耗每年增长40%。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.44,0:18:04.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, it's quite a quite a big number.\N所以这是一个相当大的数字。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.28,0:18:06.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and it might end up being a terawatt one day.\N也许有一天，它会达到太瓦级别。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.04,0:18:10.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so, this is this is serious tonnage.\N所以，这确实是一笔巨大的算力规模。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.20,0:18:11.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Awesome.\N太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.20,0:18:19.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and Tom, uh Anthropic, uh your your company, you're co-founder of Anthropic, you announced Opus 5.5 in the last several days.\N汤姆，你是Anthropic的联合创始人，最近几天你们公司宣布了Opus 5.5。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.00,0:18:23.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I thought maybe we'd go to the exponential that we are on.\N我觉得我们可以探讨一下我们正处在一个怎样的指数级增长阶段。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.92,0:18:29.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think it's helpful to ground what can Opus 5.5, and maybe it's for everybody,\N我认为，了解Opus 5.5能做什么，对每个人都有帮助，
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.06,0:18:34.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,what can Opus 5.5 do to make the lives of ordinary Americans better today?\NOpus 5.5今天能为普通美国人的生活带来哪些实际改善？
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.84,0:18:37.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And where are we going to be in a year?\N一年后我们又会走到哪里？
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.80,0:18:38.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah,\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.59,0:18:45.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,so um Opus 5.5 is uh a model that I think just continues the normal progress that we've\N所以啊，Opus 5.5 是一个我认为持续了我们正常进展的模型
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.25,0:18:53.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,had of getting kind of more IQ points for each of these superintelligences uh with each model release.\N每次模型发布，这些超级智能的智商都能提升一些。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.25,0:18:57.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and so the main things that people will see if they use it now is that it can\N嗯，现在使用它，人们主要会看到的是，它能够
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.29,0:19:03.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,do a task that takes a longer time than they'd be able to delegate to to a previous model.\N执行一项比他们之前模型能处理的更长时间的任务。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.28,0:19:07.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um And so I think the things that people should see is just like as a normal American, if you want a task,\N嗯，我觉得普通人应该明白，就像普通美国人一样，如果你有个任务，
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.80,0:19:12.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,if you want to actually delegate a task to it, it will be able to do that better is one thing.\N如果你想真正把它委派一项任务，它能更好地完成，这是其中一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.40,0:19:15.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then two is a thing that I think people notice less,\N然后第二点是人们较少注意到的事情，
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.58,0:19:20.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,which is just that there's going to be a huge amount of software being written by these models.\N也就是说，将会有大量软件由这些模型编写。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.40,0:19:27.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so all of the products that people use are going to be getting higher quality, cheaper over time.\N因此，人们所使用的所有产品都将随着时间推移变得质量更高、价格更低。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.17,0:19:35.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it'll have this effect of just like all of the all of the tools that we use now were written by like people doing engineering work.\N而且它会产生这样的效果：我们现在使用的各种工具，都是由从事工程工作的人编写出来的。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.01,0:19:44.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And now it's going to be written by both people and super intelligences doing much, much more engineering work than was possible before.\N现在，这项工作将由人类和超级智能共同完成，其工程工作量远超以往任何可能。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.36,0:19:47.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,Absolutely, but I think it's doing so much more than this.\N当然，但我认为它所做的事情远不止这些。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.64,0:19:51.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's already multiple stories of AI I'm sorry,\N已经有多个关于人工智能的故事，我感到抱歉，
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.01,0:20:02.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,super intelligent super intelligence finding a life-saving drug that can be used for a a disease that it wasn't understood that it could safely treat.\N超级智能发现了能够治疗一种此前未被理解的疾病的安全药物。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.68,0:20:03.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it's saving lives.\N所以它正在拯救生命。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.64,0:20:07.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think it's having profound impacts on education, but maybe each of you could talk.\N我认为它对教育产生了深远影响，但也许你们每个人都可以谈谈。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.86,0:20:13.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,For ordinary Americans, what's super intelligence doing today and what's it going to be able to do in a year?\N对普通美国人来说，超级智能今天在做什么，一年后又能做什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.96,0:20:16.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm an ordinary American.\N我就是一名普通美国人。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.60,0:20:27.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I use I use uh Claude to help me do research and and instead of giving me just answers in most of my research,\N我使用 Claude 帮助我进行研究，而不是只给我答案，大多数情况下，
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.19,0:20:34.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,that maybe there's comparative research that I'm doing and there's two or three different approaches to something and I wanted to answer\N比如我在做比较研究，有两三种不同的方法应对某个问题，我想回答
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.24,0:20:42.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,a list of different questions and compare and contrast rates of rates of growth or rates of change or whatever it is.\N一系列不同问题，比较和对比增长率、变化率，或者其他相关指标。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.20,0:20:46.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and so I describe literally, you know, every single question I have.\N我会逐字描述我所有的疑问。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.72,0:20:51.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,And nothing gives me more joy than and then and I ask it to create a nice report and and plot it out.\N没有什么比这更让我开心的了，然后我让它生成一份漂亮的报告并绘制出来。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.61,0:20:54.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,And sometimes it's a pie chart, sometimes it's a bar graph.\N有时是饼图，有时是条形图。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.53,0:20:55.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I just hit enter.\N然后我就按了回车键。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.92,0:21:02.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And nothing gives me more joy than just watch it go And then it comes back and it creates a beautiful, you know, beautiful report.\N没有什么比看着它运行然后回来，生成一份非常漂亮、令人惊叹的报告更让我开心的了。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.84,0:21:07.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and then instead of instead of researching all these different topics for four six eight hours,\N然后我就不必再花四到六到八小时去研究这些不同的主题了，
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.72,0:21:11.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,which back in the old days I would on a weekend, and I'll learn something new.\N就像过去周末我常做的那样，现在我还能学到新东西。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.86,0:21:19.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,It goes off and creates me this really, really beautiful final report in about 3 minutes.\N它运行起来，大约三分钟就为我生成了一份非常非常漂亮的最终报告。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.24,0:21:24.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,And, you know, it's all condensed and now you're getting smarter faster.\N而且所有内容都高度浓缩，现在你变得越来越聪明，速度更快。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.08,0:21:26.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Love it.\N太喜欢了。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.24,0:21:27.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,What about for you?\N你呢？
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.16,0:21:31.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,How was How How do you How are you seeing superintelligence helping ordinary Americans?\N你觉得超级智能会如何帮助普通美国人？
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.01,0:21:34.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,What do you think it'll do in a year or two?\N你认为它一两年后会带来什么改变？
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.88,0:21:35.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Maybe a year or two.\N或许一两年后。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.56,0:21:37.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Take the year or two from now.\N从现在起的一两年后。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.64,0:21:43.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, well, I I I think it's it's helping people organize their lives and do better at their jobs.\N是的，我觉得它确实帮助人们更好地规划生活，在工作中表现得更出色。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.21,0:21:47.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, I think it really will become um essential, if it isn't already,\N所以我认为，如果还没成为必需品的话，它很快就会变得必不可少，
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.87,0:21:55.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,for people to use AI uh for in their professional lives, certainly, and and in their private lives.\N尤其是在专业领域，当然也包括个人生活。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.23,0:21:59.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, AI is just an incredibly helpful, useful thing.\N因此，AI 简直是极其有用、非常有帮助的工具。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.92,0:22:07.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um you know, I I I've heard many anecdotes of AI helping people uh with medical issues,\N你知道，我听过很多关于 AI 帮助人们解决医疗问题的轶事，
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.92,0:22:19.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,um and many cases where the the doctor was wrong and the they they submitted their x-rays or MRI to to AI and and AI got it right.\N有很多案例中，医生判断错误，而他们把 X 光片或核磁共振影像提交给 AI，AI 却给出了正确诊断。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:19.12,0:22:21.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and but but for AI, they would have died.\N如果没有 AI，他们可能已经去世了。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:21.96,0:22:23.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I've heard many such cases.\N我听过很多类似的情况。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.88,0:22:24.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,Awesome.\N太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:24.83,0:22:30.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And hopefully Opus 5.6 tells Tom, "Don't take that left.\N希望 Opus 5.6 告诉汤姆：“别走左边，”
Dialogue: 0,0:22:30.12,0:22:31.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Take the right."\N走右边。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:31.64,0:22:34.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's what I hope.\N这正是我希望的。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:34.36,0:22:41.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think it's important these these superintelligences, they're imbued with the values of their creators.\N我认为这些超级智能必须承载其创造者的价值观。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:41.20,0:22:45.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we do have There There are American values that we all share.\N我们确实拥有全美共享的美国价值观。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:45.33,0:22:50.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,The First Amendment, free speech, commitment to truth.\N第一修正案，言论自由，对真理的承诺。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:50.68,0:22:55.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Can you Can you talk about what each of you are doing to imbue\N你们每个人能谈谈自己在如何赋予
Dialogue: 0,0:22:55.63,0:23:02.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Help make sure that these these superintelligences are imbued with with the right values.\N这些超级智能正确价值观方面所做的努力吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:23:02.84,0:23:04.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Are we allowed to say anything controversial?\N我们能说一些有争议的话吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:23:04.60,0:23:06.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Say something controversial.\N说点有争议的内容。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:06.72,0:23:12.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, so so um I it the the SIs are our tools.\N好的，那么呃，这些超级智能是我们的工具。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:13.00,0:23:19.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and the challenge with an SI with values uh meaning it has judgment.\N而超级智能带有价值观的挑战在于，它具备判断力。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:20.03,0:23:30.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um depending on how you use that SI, it may decide uh um how it decide it may judge you and its effectiveness would be affected by that judgment.\N取决于你如何使用这个超级智能，它可能会对你的行为做出判断，而这种判断会影响它的表现效果。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:30.86,0:23:39.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so it's a little bit like a steak knife where if you if you uh were served medium well, it cuts perfectly.\N这有点像一把牛排刀，如果你点的是五分熟牛排，它能完美切割。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.92,0:23:48.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,But if you were served rare steak and it looks awfully like live meat, somehow it doesn't cut.\N但如果你点的是三分熟牛排，看起来像活肉一样，不知为何它就切不动了。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.05,0:23:57.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so I I think there's a there's a there's a there's a question in my mind yet about how much judgment you really want these tools to have.\N所以我认为，关于这些工具究竟应该拥有多少判断力，我心中仍存有疑问。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:57.81,0:24:05.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and so the the the intentions of the user um I you know obviously I use it I use the knife as an example,\N用户的意图，比如我用刀作为例子，显然我使用它，
Dialogue: 0,0:24:05.69,0:24:08.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,but you can think of a whole bunch of other examples.\N但你也可以想到其他很多类似的例子。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:08.23,0:24:15.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh the intentions are a little bit different, you know, whether you're a defender or an attacker, for example, in cybersecurity.\N意图会有些不同，比如在网络安全领域，你是防御者还是攻击者。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:15.44,0:24:19.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um the defender's actions could resemble an attacker.\N防御者的行动可能看起来像攻击者。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:19.56,0:24:30.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you want the defender you want this SI to um uh activate on behalf of the defender even though it appears to be an you know an aggressive action.\N你希望这个 SI 能代表防御者采取行动，即使它看起来像是一个激进的行为。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:31.00,0:24:31.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:24:31.72,0:24:39.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think we're running up on time, but maybe if you guys could share if you spent a lot of time at the White House, is there an-\N我觉得时间快到了，不过如果你们在白宫待过很长时间，能不能分享一下——
Dialogue: 0,0:24:39.50,0:24:46.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,anything that that you can share share with the world about what came out of what was evidently a a uh a long and productive lunch?\N你们能告诉世界，那次显然漫长而富有成效的午餐最终达成了什么成果吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:24:47.00,0:24:47.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,We did good.\N我们做得不错。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:47.84,0:24:48.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:48.84,0:24:54.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,We we we signed a joint declaration uh regarding SI safety.\N我们签署了一份关于 SI 安全的联合声明。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:55.04,0:25:00.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and uh I think I think that'll be published by the White House soon, if it hasn't been already.\N嗯，我觉得白宫很快就会发布这份文件，如果还没发布的话。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:00.44,0:25:10.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, but uh, we we agreed to a to a number of things that uh, include joint monitoring, um, or special committees, and um, just generally uh,\N嗯，但我们同意了一些事项，包括联合监督、设立特别委员会，以及一般性的，
Dialogue: 0,0:25:10.66,0:25:17.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,grading each other's homework, which is a lot better than if people just grade their own homework, uh, for obvious reasons.\N互相批改作业，这比大家各自批改自己的作业要好得多，原因显而易见。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:17.60,0:25:25.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it And it includes every It includes everything from um, rigorous internal controls, um, well-established methods,\N它涵盖了从严格的内部管控、成熟的方法，
Dialogue: 0,0:25:25.28,0:25:31.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,well-established processes, um, very clearly documented intentions of the products that you're building,\N成熟的流程，以及你们所构建产品意图的清晰文档记录，
Dialogue: 0,0:25:31.33,0:25:38.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,internal controls to make sure that you're delivering on those intentions, um, internal audit, um, that that escalates uh,\N内部管控以确保实现这些意图，内部审计，以及能够向上级汇报的机制，
Dialogue: 0,0:25:38.75,0:25:45.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,external audits, um, from from a third party, and uh, um, and then industry sharing best practices.\N第三方的外部审计，以及行业内的最佳实践共享。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:46.02,0:25:51.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I thought the the um, the the declaration has has has a lot of teeth.\N我觉得这份联合声明很有分量。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:51.22,0:26:00.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, I thought it was really well written, and um, I think this is a a practice that that quite frankly has a standards for our industry going forward,\N我认为它写得非常出色，而且我认为这将为我们的行业未来设定标准，
Dialogue: 0,0:26:00.30,0:26:02.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,um, every every single company out to out to embrace.\N每一家公司都应采纳这一做法。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:03.00,0:26:06.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, uh, Podesta Podesta pulled it all together.\N所以，波德斯塔把这一切都整合起来了。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:06.36,0:26:14.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, he he um, watched over the meeting, and uh, was able to bring everybody out, and um, you know, I thought it was it was really well run.\N他全程监督了会议，成功让各方都参与进来，我觉得这场会议组织得非常好。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:14.68,0:26:15.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Awesome.\N太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:15.16,0:26:17.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, on behalf of all Americans,\N作为所有美国人的代表，
Dialogue: 0,0:26:17.11,0:26:24.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,thank thank all of you for doing everything you can to make the future as awesome and optimistic for American Americans as you can, and you are.\N感谢你们所有人尽一切努力，让美国的未来尽可能美好和充满希望，你们做到了。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:24.53,0:26:25.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, thank you.\N所以，谢谢你们。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:25.40,0:26:26.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.\N谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:26.44,0:26:29.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.\N谢谢。
